From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:55:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: shell zone
 and CPU backstop

- shell-thermal: stock's gear policy as a kernel thermal zone on a
  weighted-thermal-sensor over skin, board and charge-pump thermistors
  (stock's "front" shell model at steady state, positive terms only;
  its gain and offset are folded into the trips). One passive trip per
  stock gear that changes a CPU or GPU cap (gears 3-14, stock's entry
  temperatures and leave hysteresis), each mapping cpufreq-cpu0,
  cpufreq-cpu6 and the GPU to exactly that gear's cooling state.
  Brightness and charge caps stay in userspace: the ktz8869 and battmgr
  cooling devices have no DT node to map.
- A 95 C passive backstop trip on every CPU junction zone (step-wise
  from no limit), below stock's 105 C; denialwm's 405aa6965e8e is the
  idea, the values are ours.

Generated by wf/cmpimpl/scripts/gen-thermal-dt.py from the public stock
tables of iceland-thermal and the decoded model in iceland-firmware.

Promoted to the default device tree after the q91e opt-in rows passed
(7 Nov 2026, owner rule: what passes becomes the default).

Suggested-by: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Based-on: denialwm/linux-perpetua 405aa6965e8e (idea; the values are ours)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
